Description: Fix CVE-2026-55698 — verify npm registry signature before executing package-manager switch
 Malicious repositories could steer automatic package-manager version switching
 to install and spawn attacker-controlled pnpm bytes (via committed lockfile
 metadata and/or repository-controlled registry settings). This patch adds
 verifyPnpmEngineIdentity(), which validates npm registry signatures on staged
 pnpm/@pnpm/exe installs against embedded npm public keys before linking them
 into the tools directory and spawning. installPnpmToTools() also isolates the
 bootstrap install from workspace discovery (--ignore-workspace) and disables
 recursive version switching in the child process.
 .
 Backport of the package-manager identity verification shipped in pnpm 10.34.2
 (tools/plugin-commands-self-updater). The upstream env-lockfile force-refresh
 path (resolvePackageManagerIntegrities force:true) is not present on the
 10.32.x line; signature verification is the released mitigation for this CVE
 on 10.x. Use together with the CVE-2026-55697 trusted-registry patch for
 complete bootstrap hardening.
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/pnpm/pnpm/releases/tag/v10.34.2
Bug: https://github.com/pnpm/pnpm/security/advisories/GHSA-w466-c33r-3gjp
